    "sourceGaps": [
      "The prompt refers to available reagents without printing a full inventory. The printed key includes the original identification and dye reaction diagrams, including its II/e) notation and all yellow-orange/red/red-orange observations.",
      "Archive/compiler teaching source: The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads, Volume 1, edited by Anton Sirota, IChO International Information Centre, Bratislava, Slovakia; ©2008 IUVENTA. Attributed parts may be used for unlimited teaching; Not for sale. The editorial preface describes recreated texts/schemes/pictures and expanded or recalculated early keys. This is not an obtained original jury packet or a blanket commercial grant.",
      "The answer sheet is printed within SOLUTION. Its numerical fields remain blank. It asks for dilution in 200.0 cm³, while the subsequent method gives 5 cm³ of 2 M solution to 100 cm³. The answer-sheet mercury equation differs from the method equation; both native versions are retained. No measured titration volumes, concentrations or masses are supplied.",
      "Archive/compiler teaching source: The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads, Volume 1, edited by Anton Sirota, IChO International Information Centre, Bratislava, Slovakia; ©2008 IUVENTA. Attributed parts may be used for unlimited teaching; Not for sale. The editorial preface describes recreated texts/schemes/pictures and expanded or recalculated early keys. This is not an obtained original jury packet or a blanket commercial grant.",
      "The printed identification array and equation/observation table are retained literally. Several equations are unbalanced, including FeSO₄+H₂O₂→2 Fe(OH)SO₄ and the listed Fe(OH)₂ oxidation; the source also prints MnMnO₃. These native expressions are not silently corrected.",
